### Q1 — The Diff (`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)`)

1. **Is the deletion right and complete? (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **Yes.** In [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L653-L705), deleting `INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` leaves CPU `IRQ3` (`COP0_CAUSE & 0x800`) driven solely by [`jazz_interrupt_assert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L138-L145), [`jazz_interrupt_deassert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L147-L155), and the [`case R4030_SYS_EXT_IMASK:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L454-L470) write arm in [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L334-L539).
   - No other site in [dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c) touches `d->mips_irq_3`, `d->int_asserted`, or `d->int_enable_mask` (`READ`: lines 1–799).

2. **Comment accuracy in Section 1 ([apply_fix578b.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/apply_fix578b.py#L9-L17)) (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **Change 1 — Four phrases in the Section 1 comment need widening/correction** (all four are already fixed in the working-tree comment at [dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L696-L702)):
     1. *"until some line was asserted anew"*: **Widen it.** If `R4030_EXT_IP3` (`0x0002`, [pica.h](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/pica.h#L97)) transitions `0 -> 1` on a guest write to `R4030_SYS_EXT_IMASK` while `d->int_asserted & 0x7fff` is non-zero, [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L466-L469) re-asserts `d->mips_irq_3` (`!old_assert_3 && new_assert_3`) without any device line being asserted anew (`READ` / `REASONED`). By contrast, periodic ticks in [`DEVICE_TICK(jazz)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L295-L308) and [`DEVICE_TICK(ns16550)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_ns16550.c#L96) heal *by* calling `INTERRUPT_ASSERT(...)` (asserting a line anew).
     2. *"so a vector read taken with a second JAZZ line still pending"*: **Too narrow.** The deleted tail executed unconditionally on **every** access to `pica_jazzio` (offsets `0`, `2`, and `default:`, both `MEM_READ` and `MEM_WRITE`), and dropped `IRQ3` whenever **any** JAZZ line `0..14` was still pending — including when only **one** line was pending and its device ISR had not yet cleared the source (as `jz ip onevec` demonstrates) (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     3. *"which recompute it from the pending lines and the enable mask on every change"*: **Imprecise.** [`jazz_interrupt_assert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L143-L144) only asserts (no `else` branch), [`jazz_interrupt_deassert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L153-L154) only deasserts (without consulting `d->int_enable_mask`), and [`case R4030_SYS_EXT_IMASK:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L466-L469) is transition-gated (`old_assert_3` vs `new_assert_3`). Together they *keep the CPU line equal to* `(d->int_asserted & 0x7fff) && (d->int_enable_mask & R4030_EXT_IP3)` rather than each site performing a standalone recompute like [`reassert_isa_interrupts()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L130-L135) (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     4. *"a read has no side effect, as in the tree's other interrupt controllers"*: **False as a tree-wide claim.** Even within [dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L439-L444), reading `R4030_SYS_IT_STAT` deasserts `d->jazz_timer_irq` as a read side effect (`READ`). Keep the working-tree wording in [dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L696-L702), which drops that clause and repairs all four items.

