### Q2 — Ruling D1 (`if (!(d->int_asserted & 0x7fff))` vs Deletion)

1. **Prior preference (`READ`):** We were not on the Pass 1 panel roster.
2. **Does any argument for the conditional survive? (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **No.** Let $P \equiv (\text{d->int\_asserted} \mathbin{\&} \text{0x7fff} \neq 0)$, $E \equiv (\text{d->int\_enable\_mask} \mathbin{\&} \text{R4030\_EXT\_IP3} \neq 0)$, and $I \equiv (\text{COP0\_CAUSE} \mathbin{\&} \text{0x800} \neq 0)$.
   - [`mips_cpu_interrupt_deassert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips.c#L1885-L1894) executes `cpu->cd.mips.coproc[0]->reg[COP0_CAUSE] &= ~interrupt->line;` (`line == 0x800`), which mutates state iff $I$ holds (`READ`).
   - Therefore `if (!P) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` has an observable effect iff $(\neg P \land I)$ holds at the tail of `DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)` (`REASONED`).
   - By induction over the exhaustive writer census in `GXEMUL-SEC/src`:
     - Initial state: `CHECK_ALLOCATION(malloc(sizeof(struct jazz_data)))` + `memset(d, 0, ...)` ([dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L717-L718)) and `memset(cp, 0, sizeof(struct mips_coproc))` ([cpu_mips_coproc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_coproc.c#L360-L361)) establish $\neg P \land \neg E \land \neg I$, so $I \iff (P \land E)$ holds initially (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     - [`jazz_interrupt_assert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L138-L145) sets a bit in `0x7fff` ($P' = \text{true}$) and asserts `mips_irq_3` iff $E$, preserving $I' \iff (P' \land E)$ (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     - [`jazz_interrupt_deassert()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L147-L155) clears a bit in `0x7fff` and deasserts `mips_irq_3` when `!P'`, preserving $I' \iff (P' \land E)$ (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     - [`case R4030_SYS_EXT_IMASK:`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L454-L470) computes `old_assert_3 = P && E_old` and `new_assert_3 = P && E_new` and asserts/deasserts on transitions, preserving $I' \iff (P \land E')$ (`READ` / `REASONED`).
     - Guest `mtc0` to `COP0_CAUSE` in [`coproc_register_write()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_mips_coproc.c#L951-L955) masks with `MIPS_SR_INT_MASK_0 | MIPS_SR_INT_MASK_1` (`0x300`), leaving `0x800` untouched (`READ`).
   - Thus $I \iff (P \land E)$ is an exact invariant across all guest-reachable executions, making $\neg P \land I$ unreachable (`REASONED`). The conditional adds dead code that only diverges if a host operator manually pokes `cause = 0x800` via the debugger [`reg_cmd()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger_cmds.c#L1432-L1498), while breaking twin byte-identity if upgraded to `!(P && E)`. Rulings D1 and D2 are sound.

