### Q3 — The Floor (Escapes of the 22-Row Probe & Table 2 Completeness)

1. **Is the `(d)` enumeration in Table 2 complete over `DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)`'s own tests? (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **No.** [`DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio)`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L666-L694) tests:
     - `switch (relative_addr)`: `case 0:` (`:667`), `case 2:` (`:679`), `default:` (`:685`, i.e. `relative_addr != 0 && relative_addr != 2`, which in a 4-byte window `DEV_JAZZIO_LENGTH = 0x4` at `:69, :786` means `relative_addr == 1 || relative_addr == 3`).
     - `if (writeflag == MEM_WRITE)` inside `case 2:` (`:680`, plus its implicit `else` `writeflag == MEM_READ`) and inside `default:` (`:686`, plus `else` at `:690`).
   - Table 2 (`M_offs0`, `M_offsne0`, `M_rd`, `M_wr`, `M_offs2`) omits:
     - `relative_addr != 2` (dual of `M_offs2`),
     - `relative_addr != 0 && relative_addr != 2` (the `default:` arm itself, or `relative_addr == 1` / `relative_addr == 3` / `relative_addr & 1`),
     - the function's compound branch cells `{case 0, case 2, default} x {MEM_READ, MEM_WRITE}`.
   - **Critically (`READ` / `REASONED`):** In the 22-row probe ([jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable2_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L226-L249)), the `(default, MEM_WRITE)` cell is **not rowed at all** (`jz ip dflt` reads offset `1`; nothing writes offset `1` or `3`). That makes the 22-row probe's own header contract (*"Every access path through DEVICE_ACCESS(jazz_jazzio) -- offsets 0 and 2 and the default arm, read and write -- is rowed with lines pending"*, lines 38–40) **false**.

2. **Smallest re-introductions at the deleted site that score 22/22 on the 22-row probe and change guest-visible `IRQ3` (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **Change 2 — Close the single-variable and compound branch escapes below** (all five are closed by the 26-row working-tree [jazz_vector_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/jazz_vector_probe.py#L254-L287) and verified in [PRETABLE3.out](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable3_20261102/PRETABLE3.out)):
     1. **Keyed to `idata`:** `if (idata) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);`
        - In the 22-row probe, `idata == 0` on every read ([dev_jazz.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L660)) and on both writes (`st32(VEC, 0)` in `jz ip vecw` and `st8(VEC + 2, 0)` in `jz ip lbiew`), so it scores **22/22**, yet drops `IRQ3` whenever a guest writes a non-zero local-bus interrupt enable mask to `PICA_SYS_LB_IE` (`0xe0000002`, e.g. OpenBSD `pica_intr_establish`).
     2. **Keyed to `d->jazz_timer_value`:** `if (d->jazz_timer_value) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);`
        - `d->jazz_timer_value` stays `0` throughout all 22 rows, scoring **22/22**, yet drops `IRQ3` on **every** `pica_jazzio` access once a guest writes a non-zero `LB_IE` mask.
     3. **Keyed to `relative_addr` alone:** `if (relative_addr == 3) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` (or `if (relative_addr > 2)`)
        - Offset `3` of the 4-byte `pica_jazzio` window is never accessed in the 22-row probe (**22/22**).
     4. **Keyed to `relative_addr` and `writeflag` (the enclosing function's own `default:` write arm at `:686`):** `if (relative_addr & writeflag) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` (since `MEM_WRITE == 1`, `MEM_READ == 0`) or `if (relative_addr != 0 && relative_addr != 2 && writeflag == MEM_WRITE) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);`
        - Scores **22/22** on the 22-row probe because `(default, write)` is unrowed.
     5. **Keyed to `len` (and `relative_addr`):**
        - `if (len == 2) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` — no 16-bit access is performed in the 22-row probe (**22/22**), even though `PICA_SYS_LB_IE` at offset `2` is a 16-bit register (`dev_jazz.c:679`).
        - `if (!relative_addr && len == 1) INTERRUPT_DEASSERT(d->mips_irq_3);` — in the 22-row probe, offset `0` is only accessed with `ld32`/`st32` (`len == 4`), so this scores **22/22**, yet OpenBSD's `pica_iointr()` reads `PICA_SYS_LB_IS` via `inb(PVIS)` (`len == 1`) and therefore suffers the exact HEAD bug!

