### Q4 — The Vehicle ([jazz_vector_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/jazz_vector_probe.py) & [gate_mips.NEW.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/gate_mips.NEW.sh))

1. **Load-sensitivity & skipped-store hazard (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **Device tick boundary:** Both [`DEV_NS16550_TICKSHIFT`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_ns16550.c#L50) and [`DEV_JAZZ_TICKSHIFT`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_jazz.c#L63) are `14` ($2^{14} = 16,384$ instructions per tick), and entering [`debugger()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger.c#L800) calls `timer_stop()`. Even the 26-row probe executes only `40` single-stepped instructions (`> 400x` below the first periodic tick), so host CPU load cannot trigger an asynchronous `DEVICE_TICK` re-assertion (`READ` / `REASONED`).
   - **Change 3 — Skipped-step false-pass hazard in the 22-row vehicle:** In the 22-row [jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/artifacts/jazzvecdeassert/killtable2_20261102/jazz_vector_probe.ASRUN.py#L129-L171), `wait()` returns `False` on wall-clock timeout without setting `self.dead = True`, and `exec_stub()` ignores `None` returns from `set_reg()` and `send("step")`. If a `step` on a guest `VEC` access (`ld32(VEC)`, `st32(VEC, 0)`, etc.) times out under extreme host stall, the `VEC` access is skipped while `COP0_CAUSE` retains `0x800` from the preceding `reheal()`, so the subsequent `ip3()` read sees `0x800` and logs a **false `ok`**! In addition, [gate_mips.NEW.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/_scratchpad/w578/gate_mips.NEW.sh#L83-L84) checks `JAZZVEC_RESULT=` instead of `JAZZVEC_DONE` and does not pass `JAZZVEC_LOG="$LOGDIR/..."` (leaking logs to `/tmp/jazzvec_<pid>.log`).
   - **Working-tree status (`READ`):** The 26-row [jazz_vector_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/jazz_vector_probe.py#L168-L197) and [gate_mips.sh](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/gate_mips.sh#L69-L108) add `self.bad = True` on any failed `wait()` / `read_reg()`, emit `JAZZVEC_DRIVER=ok`, require `JAZZVEC_DONE`, and set `JAZZVEC_LOG="$LOGDIR/jazz_vector_probe.log"`. One small residual wart remains in [`Emu.wait()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/jazz_vector_probe.py#L163-L165): on timeout it sets `self.bad = True` and returns `False`, but does not set `self.dead = True`, so subsequent `send()` calls still run and wait 15 s each (or consume a late prompt) instead of short-circuiting immediately.

2. **Padded-column hazard in `gate_mips.sh` (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - **No hazard.** `row()` formats the name with `%-14s` followed by a literal space (`"  %-14s %-16s %s\n"`, [jazz_vector_probe.py](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/jazz_vector_probe.py#L228)), producing `15 - len(name)` spaces after `name`. Every row name in both the 22-row and 26-row probes has `len(name) <= 13` (longest: `jz ip maskoff` and `jz vec masked` at 13 chars $\rightarrow$ 2 spaces), so `grep -q "^  $v  .*ok$"` matches every row and prevents prefix collisions such as `jz vec` (9 spaces) matching `jz vec again` or `jz vec byte` (1 space after `jz vec`) (`READ` / `REASONED`).

3. **Late-answer / misparse hazard (`READ` / `REASONED`)**
   - Under non-timed-out operation, [`debugger_read_line()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger.c#L380) prints `"GXemul> "` strictly synchronously after [`debugger_execute_cmd()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/debugger/debugger.c#L868) completes, and neither the commands sent nor their output contain `"GXemul>"` (`READ`).
   - Aside from setting `self.dead = True` on `wait()` timeout above, note that in [`Emu.read_reg()`](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/regress/jazz_vector_probe.py#L188-L191) the fallback `idx = out.find(name)` always matches the echoed `"print <name>"` line first; deleting the fallback and relying solely on `re.search(rf"{re.escape(name)}\s*=\s*0x([0-9a-fA-F]+)", out)` is cleaner (`READ` / `REASONED`).

